WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.103
The lasting takeaway is that scale-equivariance
should be treated as a signal-processing problem.

00:00:06.183 --> 00:00:08.717
Once you formulate down-scaling as ideal,

00:00:08.797 --> 00:00:15.856
anti-aliased downsampling and require every output
frequency to depend only on equal or lower input frequencies,

00:00:15.936 --> 00:00:20.829
you can build networks from Fourier layers that are
exactly scale-equivariant,

00:00:20.909 --> 00:00:26.693
with provably zero error rather than the small
residual errors that plagued earlier methods.

00:00:26.773 --> 00:00:32.112
And this theoretical guarantee comes at no
practical cost: the model matches or beats

00:00:32.192 --> 00:00:36.446
prior scale-equivariant CNNs on accuracy and is
more data-efficient,

00:00:36.526 --> 00:00:39.060
especially on challenging natural images.
